  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 103.37 Man-made drainage ditch",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 103.37 “Man-made drainage ditch” means, for purposes of RSA 482-A:3, IV(b), a narrow channel dug in the ground for drainage, located in uplands above the permanent water table.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 103.35)",
